    "kernel": "The closed bounded first-order grammar accepts only the pinned function arities/signatures and listed outer variables. Integer witness types, binder-capture exclusion, exact body rendering and full old-case inverse are checked before any output directory is created. The nineteen source slices and seven full physical containers are bound; no new axiom, theorem premise or statement-mask dispatch is introduced.",
    "original_full_antecedent": "OwnedEffects::world(h,owners,ready) && Owners::active_owner(owners,l) && Owners::active_owner(owners,r) && OwnedEffects::is_ready(ready,l) && OwnedEffects::is_ready(ready,r) && OwnedEffects::header(h,l,bl,nl,cl) && OwnedEffects::header(h,r,br,nr,cr) && Heap::automatic_available(h,24,8,a)",
    "other_case": "The size/capacity witnesses read the original h,observed field functions, never the desired post-state. Their well-typedness is unconditional; proving the stronger preservation target still requires the unchanged full A and Q. No global owner validity or desired header postcondition is inserted as a new premise.",
    "self_swap": "The two equality guards deliberately overlap when l==r. Both old full-source header predicates remain in A; since their Integer cells at offsets8/16 are equal, constructor injectivity identifies nl=nr and cl=cr in that self case. The exact temporary/copy/copy/copy/end_automatic source definition is unchanged. This does not relax original C separated contracts or grant source self-swap eligibility.",
    "sufficient_rule": "Each witness has integer sort and free variables confined to the unchanged outer universal binders. Capture-free simultaneous substitution gives Header(w_size,w_capacity), which entails the old two-integer existential by ordinary existential introduction. No proof of Header is assumed or inferred from this construction.",
